Summary: Check the dependency tree for jackson-databind

Reasoning:
Okay, so my first thought is about this `task-web/pom.xml`. I see it's pulling in `spring-boot-starter-webmvc`, and I know that automatically brings in `jackson-databind` as a transitive dependency. The key thing here is the `spring-boot-starter-parent` version, which is currently `4.0.6`. My immediate concern is whether this particular version of the parent POM is still managing a vulnerable version of 
`jackson-databind`. If it is, I'm going to have to step in and explicitly override it to a secure version.

To figure out exactly what version is being resolved, my next logical step is to run `mvn dependency:tree`. That command will give me a clear picture of the dependency hierarchy and, crucially, the exact version of `jackson-databind` that's actually being included in my project. Once I have that, I can compare it against known vulnerabilities and make the necessary adjustments.

